From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:15:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Linux host: movie::Decoder decodes (VP8 / VP9 by libvpx,
 Vorbis by stb_vorbis) and a probe plays a RomFS movie through the SDK's own
 extractor

horizon_movie.py follows the Mach host's protocol (inputs, output slots, four events, SDK 3 constructor numbering); linux/host/movie.c decodes (libvpx loaded at run time). The SDK's Extractor is left to run as lifted code. movie_probe.py (NX2LINUX_MOVIE_PROBE) verifies against ffmpeg: Xenoblade 2's movies come out picture for picture identical. Without the decoders the openings are still refused explicitly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: NX2Linux milestone E: the game's movies decode (the Decoder behind the SDK's movie player was a stub answering 0)
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch Téo/jalon-e-audio-saves-video)

